      "automation_source": "clawsweeper",
      "repair_reason": "- No automated repair is needed; a maintainer should accept the provider-routing compatibility change and select this viable branch as canonical.; Cleared: The patch adds no dependency, permission, secret, workflow, or new execution surface; approval classification remains host-run, bounded, and fail-closed, with existing mutation gates unchanged. (sha=ecaac8ded060795ed9acd2292cd37645e513fb73)",
      "review_summary": "Routes Crestodian’s ambiguous approval-intent classifier through the configured `utilityModel`, adds regression coverage, and updates utility-model docs, schema help, and type comments.\n\nPR surface: Source +4, Tests +11, Docs 0. Total +15 across 7 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. at source level. An ambiguous reply reaches `classifyCrestodianApprovalIntent`, current main omits the utility-routing flag, and the shared selector demonstrably maps that flag to the configured utility model; this read-only review did not run a paid live provider completion.",
